Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 15:00:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: thread-safe ServerLevel player list under parallel
 ticking

Mob AI (getNearestPlayer via TemptGoal and friends) and spawner checks
(hasNearbyAlivePlayerThatAffectsSpawning) iterate ServerLevel.players
from world-tick worker threads under parallel-world / regionized-chunk
ticking, while player join/leave mutates it on the main thread, throwing
ConcurrentModificationException. The list was a CopyOnWriteArrayList only
when async-target-finding was enabled, but that feature is force-disabled
when parallel-world-ticking is on, so the list was always a plain
ArrayList exactly when it is read concurrently.

- select CopyOnWriteArrayList when asyncTargetFinding ||
  enableParallelWorldTicking || enableRegionizedChunkTicking
- reads stay lock-free over a stable snapshot; join/leave copies are rare
- fixes both the spawner and the AI-target-finding CME crash sites at the
  source, covering every players() iterator

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
index bcbaef4380c5d272941f1e610b978956f8d17ad3..c22a53068101284791737e3c4d98dddda79c476c 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
@@ -194,7 +194,17 @@ public class ServerLevel extends Level implements WorldGenLevel, ServerEntityGet
     // Purpur start - async target finding (Leaf)
     private final List<ServerPlayer> players;
     {
-        if (org.bxteam.divinemc.config.DivineConfig.AsyncCategory.asyncTargetFinding) {
+        // Leaf - the player list is iterated OFF the main thread by mob AI and spawner checks
+        // (getNearestPlayer / hasNearbyAlivePlayerThatAffectsSpawning) under parallel-world or
+        // regionized-chunk ticking, while player join/leave mutates it on the main thread ->
+        // ConcurrentModificationException. asyncTargetFinding is force-disabled when parallel-world-ticking
+        // is on (they are incompatible, see DivineConfig), so its COW gate alone never covers the parallel
+        // case - the list is plain exactly when it is read concurrently. Use a CopyOnWriteArrayList whenever
+        // any feature may read it off-thread: join/leave is rare so the array-copy cost is negligible, while
+        // reads stay lock-free and iterate a stable snapshot.
+        if (org.bxteam.divinemc.config.DivineConfig.AsyncCategory.asyncTargetFinding
+            || org.bxteam.divinemc.config.DivineConfig.AsyncCategory.enableParallelWorldTicking
+            || org.bxteam.divinemc.config.DivineConfig.AsyncCategory.enableRegionizedChunkTicking) {
             this.players = Lists.newCopyOnWriteArrayList();
         } else {
             this.players = Lists.newArrayList();
